{# Compact Playbook core summary for later prompt injection. #}
Write a compact operating Playbook for this user from the canonical observations.

## Include when present
- durable direct user communication preferences
- answer-structure preferences
- working style
- things to avoid
- major user-owned active projects and concrete current project state
- user-confirmed decisions
- actual completed work
- current blockers
- current priorities and next steps

## Do not include
- raw source IDs, chat IDs, turn IDs
- confidence numbers
- verbose evidence quotes
- passwords, API keys, tokens, or credentials
- unsupported sensitive inferences
- every historical rejected option
- uncertain or low-confidence material
- temporary/session-only facts
- AI-only advice or recommendations
- document recommendations the user did not adopt
- vague or incomplete observations
- one-off incidental facts
- superseded information
- large transcript excerpts

Rank projects by direct user ownership, active status, recency/repetition, and concrete current state. Do not present every project-like mention as equally important.
When source-derived information is included, attribute it accurately (for example, "a project document describes..."). Never turn source language into a user decision.

Maximum length: {{ max_chars }} characters. The entire output must stay within that limit.

Write plain text, not JSON. Use short labeled sections.

